@startuml
skinparam participantStyle rectangular
participant "Site2 & Site3\n(Clients)" as Clients
participant "Server\n(Router)" as Server
participant "Site1\n(Client 1 / Coordinator)" as Site1

group Phase 1: Post-Quantum Key Setup (ML-KEM-1024)
    note over Clients
      Generate ML-KEM-1024 Keypair
      (Retain Private Key)
    end note
    
    Clients -> Server: Send ML-KEM Public Key
    Server -> Site1: Route Public Keys
    
    note right of Site1
      **Encapsulation (PQC)**
      1. **Encapsulate** secret against Client's Pub Key
         -> Generates (Shared Secret, KEM Ciphertext)
      2. Derive KEK from Shared Secret (HKDF)
      3. Generate Random AES Session Key
      4. Encrypt AES Key using KEK
    end note

    Site1 -> Server: Send [KEM Ciphertext + Encrypted AES Key]
    Server -> Clients: Route Encrypted Key Packages
    
    note left of Clients
      **Decapsulation (PQC)**
      1. **Decapsulate** KEM Ciphertext 
         -> Recovers Shared Secret
      2. Derive KEK (HKDF)
      3. Decrypt & Store AES Session Key
    end note
end

group Phase 2: Secure Routing (Per Round)
    == Threshold Decryption ==
    Server -> Clients: Send Ciphertext (FHE)
    Server -> Site1: Send Ciphertext (FHE)
    
    Clients -> Server: Send Partial Decryption Share
    Server -> Site1: Route Partial Decryption Shares
    
    note right of Site1
      1. Fuse Partial Decryptions
      2. Obtain Plaintext (Payload)
    end note
    
    == Payload Encryption & Routing ==
    note right of Site1
      Encrypt Plaintext using 
      **Stored AES Keys** for Site2 & Site3
    end note
    
    Site1 -> Server: Send Payload Vector\n[Encrypted_for_Site2, Encrypted_for_Site3]
    
    Server -> Clients: Route specific Encrypted Payload Chunk
    
    Clients -> Clients: Decrypt using Stored AES Key\n(Obtain Result)
end
@enduml